            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Results vary. Plot one dot for each sample mean on an axis labelled “Mean coin age (years)”.",
              "worked": "Collect the sample means from the class. Choose a suitable, evenly spaced scale for mean coin age in years. Plot one dot for each sample mean, stacking dots for repeated values. Compare the spread and clustering of the sample means.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 65
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-act5-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "Try this with larger samples.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Results vary. Larger samples usually produce sample means with less variation.",
              "worked": "Repeat the sampling using more than 20 coins per sample. Record each coin's age, add the ages and divide by the number of coins in that sample. Plot and compare the new sample means with those from samples of 20. The larger-sample means will usually be less spread out.",
